{
    "word": "syncretism",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "de662baf-10ad-3bcf-bcb9-925b039a262a",
                "word": "syncretism",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "12816f6a-2a2c-441d-a19c-35c90cdd6c58",
                        "entry_id": "de662baf-10ad-3bcf-bcb9-925b039a262a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "syncretisms"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "633b0f6c-b64a-3f06-9c8c-9e1dff1ce067",
                        "entry_id": "de662baf-10ad-3bcf-bcb9-925b039a262a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The reconciliation or fusion of different systems or beliefs (religious, cultural, or otherwise cosmologic or ontologic)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ef190d81-a422-42a2-a629-0bb49dcd3096",
                                "sense_id": "633b0f6c-b64a-3f06-9c8c-9e1dff1ce067",
                                "text": "Having thus established his trinity of hypotheses, M. Lamennais deduces therefrom, by a badly connected chain of analogies, his whole philosophy. And it is here especially that we notice the syncretism which is peculiar to him. The theory of M. Lamennais embraces all systems, and supports all opinions."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e023b055-40f9-4f00-b2f8-50cf353df380",
                                "sense_id": "633b0f6c-b64a-3f06-9c8c-9e1dff1ce067",
                                "text": "It provides a more natural explanation of the Colossian syncretism as stemming from local religious impulses that continued to wield a powerful draw on people converted to Christianity from the local Jewish communities and pagan cults.[…]The kind of syncretism we find at Colossae was not unique to that city or region."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "990dbb6d-58c6-4596-b832-dea87780eb9d",
                                "sense_id": "633b0f6c-b64a-3f06-9c8c-9e1dff1ce067",
                                "text": "Kraft's functional view of Anthropology eventually leads to syncretism because God is understood as working within a modern, humanistic paradigm."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5b975728-ce10-4a5c-b606-7afb68f93ba6",
                                "sense_id": "633b0f6c-b64a-3f06-9c8c-9e1dff1ce067",
                                "text": "The strategies of religious syncretism—the active transformation through renegotiation, reorganization, and redefinition of clashing belief systems—are consistent with the creolization process."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f922a1a7-a1eb-36c9-bc9e-c9b546b5aace",
                        "entry_id": "de662baf-10ad-3bcf-bcb9-925b039a262a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The fusion of different inflexional forms."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "495920ec-ab09-4465-ad40-cb076e6ca6e2",
                                "sense_id": "f922a1a7-a1eb-36c9-bc9e-c9b546b5aace",
                                "text": "In this paper a distinction is assumed between full syncretism, which affects whole morphemes, and partial syncretism, which affects only some case allomorphs, and also between syncretism proper and mere loss of a case morpheme."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "236cf6d0-0ef8-4ac1-ab28-26d568e53ae6",
                                "sense_id": "f922a1a7-a1eb-36c9-bc9e-c9b546b5aace",
                                "text": "Romanian conjugation displays several cases of syncretism, in which two paradigmatic slots share the same grammatical desinence.[…]On the other hand, the syncretisms of the imperfect and subjunctive are not phonologically conditioned and, as such, apply to every verb without exception."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1a88efea-1928-428a-8d81-a26f02ca6e7b",
                                "sense_id": "f922a1a7-a1eb-36c9-bc9e-c9b546b5aace",
                                "text": "In this chapter, I will investigate whether they deserve this name by looking at syncretisms between clusivity and other person markers."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8607dcb3-b749-42d1-9306-b80244350c35",
                        "source_entry_id": "de662baf-10ad-3bcf-bcb9-925b039a262a",
                        "source_sense_description": "fusion of different systems or beliefs",
                        "target_lang_word": "synkretismus",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "synkretismus",
                                "target_lang_code": "cs",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae47bda5-a79c-31af-b833-a150750f0e30",
                                        "entry_id": "198c9fff-07a0-3683-a308-5fd77498241f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "mechanické slučování různých prvků"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59fc4f1c-267b-44f0-8600-af9a92195b3d",
                                                "sense_id": "ae47bda5-a79c-31af-b833-a150750f0e30",
                                                "text": "Během celé té doby, kdy nadporučík Lukáš stal se velitelem jedenácté marškumpačky, ocitl se ve stavu zvaném synkretismus, to jest ve filosofii, že usiloval rozpory pojmové vyrovnávati pomocí ústupků až k smíšení názorů."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "478af5d9-9aa4-395a-a731-f8d040947bfc",
                                        "entry_id": "198c9fff-07a0-3683-a308-5fd77498241f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "splývání více pádů v jeden"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f95c8ae6-4f39-4438-b1ad-615de7853b2f",
                        "source_entry_id": "de662baf-10ad-3bcf-bcb9-925b039a262a",
                        "source_sense_description": "fusion of different systems or beliefs",
                        "target_lang_word": "syncrétisme",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "syncrétisme",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3a7d9bff-e681-31f9-a6fa-67ffd69cc9e7",
                                        "entry_id": "34845747-cff7-3efb-9ff1-5b8c72fb642d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Système de philosophie grecque qui faisait la synthèse des divers systèmes de pensée."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1fcabdb1-3cc3-41ec-8ac4-026104afd098",
                                                "sense_id": "3a7d9bff-e681-31f9-a6fa-67ffd69cc9e7",
                                                "text": "Deux circonstances expliquent le phénomène. La première fut la croyance en l’unité de la philosophie antique. Elle est due à un vaste effort de syncrétisme des dernières écoles d’Alexandrie et d’Athènes qui s’évertuèrent à coordonner le Platonisme, l’Aristotélisme, le Stoïcisme, le Néo-Pythagorisme en une synthèse unique […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7ee0f530-d657-3808-b5bd-f7fefe880f64",
                                        "entry_id": "34845747-cff7-3efb-9ff1-5b8c72fb642d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Rapprochement de divers cultes ; fusion de plusieurs doctrines religieuses."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29a33597-f1ae-4339-a965-b55208a79990",
                                                "sense_id": "7ee0f530-d657-3808-b5bd-f7fefe880f64",
                                                "text": "Il faut en effet, pour faire œuvre utile, éviter dès le départ toute confusion et prendre garde de ne pas tomber dans un syncrétisme hâtif : le syncrétisme est une dégénérescence de la pensée."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c7c18cc-57cb-44b3-81e5-3b11aee9021b",
                                                "sense_id": "7ee0f530-d657-3808-b5bd-f7fefe880f64",
                                                "text": "Quelques mois après, Claude Lévi-Strauss publia, dans Les Temps modernes, un article célèbre dans lequel il remettait la fête de Noël en perspective historique et anthropologique. Il y rappelait l’ancienneté des racines païennes comme chrétiennes de cette fête, le syncrétisme d’éléments remontant à la Rome ancienne, aux fêtes scandinaves ou au Moyen Age européen."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ddd5cf10-9de0-31b2-8d2e-2ccfb2fd2cf2",
                                        "entry_id": "34845747-cff7-3efb-9ff1-5b8c72fb642d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mélange d’opinions, de doctrines, de modes de pensée, etc. → voir métissage"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c83151a-9624-4f0b-b21b-53a3ca2a5bca",
                                                "sense_id": "ddd5cf10-9de0-31b2-8d2e-2ccfb2fd2cf2",
                                                "text": "Le royaume normand de Sicile fut un bel exemple de tolérance religieuse et de syncrétisme culturel."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8da1ab59-5f35-318f-95ff-afa288073949",
                                        "entry_id": "34845747-cff7-3efb-9ff1-5b8c72fb642d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Regroupement de plusieurs traits grammaticaux en un seul élément."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7b001469-205b-4fb5-9979-2328d315f612",
                        "source_entry_id": "de662baf-10ad-3bcf-bcb9-925b039a262a",
                        "source_sense_description": "fusion of different systems or beliefs",
                        "target_lang_word": "Synkretismus",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Synkretismus",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a68c6dab-abf2-3378-b638-0c3cc9b43680",
                                        "entry_id": "be524656-6bd3-3e56-af57-9c27a6e12f3d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "die Vermischung zweier oder mehrerer Lehren"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49695ef3-9053-4391-8e47-b96a75227fe7",
                                                "sense_id": "a68c6dab-abf2-3378-b638-0c3cc9b43680",
                                                "text": "„Das Ganze ist von einem wunderlichen mythologischen Synkretismus heimgesucht.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8fb3c57c-b753-30c3-a6af-00dd870f0b6e",
                                        "entry_id": "be524656-6bd3-3e56-af57-9c27a6e12f3d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Zusammenfall von Flexionsmorphemen innerhalb eines Paradigmas (innerparadigmatischer Synkretismus) oder über Paradigmen hinweg (transparadigmatischer Synkretismus)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8383e7ea-e271-4d2d-b43e-6e95b7e296d6",
                                                "sense_id": "8fb3c57c-b753-30c3-a6af-00dd870f0b6e",
                                                "text": "Synkretismen kommen besonders häufig in der indogermanischen Sprachfamilie vor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1b486e1-cf54-4c8d-addb-f4a351ecb806",
                                                "sense_id": "8fb3c57c-b753-30c3-a6af-00dd870f0b6e",
                                                "text": "„Der Synkretismus führte dazu, daß heute nicht mehr alle Kasus scharf voneinander geschieden werden.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "474d2687-9c1e-493d-8210-65e490f2804c",
                                                "sense_id": "8fb3c57c-b753-30c3-a6af-00dd870f0b6e",
                                                "text": "„Überraschenderweise wird beim suffigierten bestimmten Artikel der Synkretismus der Substantivflexion im Nominativ/Akkusativ Plural durch die beiden Flexive {-nir} beziehungsweise {-nar} aufgehoben.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "97383ab7-7466-3ec8-95f0-affd296f4d26",
                                        "entry_id": "be524656-6bd3-3e56-af57-9c27a6e12f3d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "die unkritische Übernahme und Verschmelzung verschiedenartiger philosophischer Ansätze in einen eher zufälligen Zusammenhang, der innere Einheit und Widerspruchslosigkeit vermissen lässt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad34c169-b5db-41d0-9fae-4ef51dc3f81c",
                                                "sense_id": "97383ab7-7466-3ec8-95f0-affd296f4d26",
                                                "text": "„Diejenigen Philosophen des 16. Jahrhunderts, die zwischen Platon und Aristoteles vermitteln wollten, wurden des Synkretismus bezichtigt.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"3\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79e7cada-0d89-3d0e-880b-c13e60723249",
                                        "entry_id": "be524656-6bd3-3e56-af57-9c27a6e12f3d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "eklektizistische Mischung religiöser Grundsätze und Lehren unterschiedlicher Herkunft"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1d0a411-adc6-4052-a97d-e5efa956c905",
                                                "sense_id": "79e7cada-0d89-3d0e-880b-c13e60723249",
                                                "text": "Der Synkretismus der New-Age-Bewegung wird häufig von den christlichen Kirchen thematisiert."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0bd14e2d-2427-43e1-b88b-9dd385ece57e",
                                                "sense_id": "79e7cada-0d89-3d0e-880b-c13e60723249",
                                                "text": "„Über den antiken Synkretismus hinaus ist Vermischung von Religionen oder Göttern ein in der Religionsgeschichte häufiges Phänomen, das notwendig dort auftritt, wo… Religionen zusammentreffen“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96c7e114-fbd7-4b87-b905-28623de5fcd5",
                                                "sense_id": "79e7cada-0d89-3d0e-880b-c13e60723249",
                                                "text": "„Eine vierte, gegenwärtig in der Forschung viel diskutierte Ursache für die Ausbreitung des Islam ist die Etablierung eines Synkretismus, in dem sich islamische und andersgläubige Versatzstücke miteinander verbanden.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"4\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
